// `ctxc check` on a directory with a build.ctx checks every executable the build program
// describes, with the file it generates and the unchecked operations it denies. An error in
// a file two executables share is reported once.
//# $ ctxc check {dir}
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/lib/lib.ctx:2:42: error: operands of `/` have incompatible types: i64 and {float}; convert one with @as
//| {work:.}/gen/one/made.ctx:1:42: error: expected i64, got bool
//| {dir}/two/main.ctx:3:13: error: `@cast` is unchecked, and `build::deny_unchecked` in build.ctx denies it here: it has no checked form, so write it in a directory its `except` lists
//| {dir}/two/main.ctx:4:46: error: expected i64, got []u8
//| check: 4 errors; not checked until the program has no other error: the order of a call's fields, what tasks borrow, consts computed by running code

// The build program is built and run to say what there is to check, and no executable is.
//# list {work:.}:
//| build
//| gen

// `run` stops at the first executable with an error.
//# $ ctxc run {dir}
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/lib/lib.ctx:2:42: error: operands of `/` have incompatible types: i64 and {float}; convert one with @as
//| {work:.}/gen/one/made.ctx:1:42: error: expected i64, got bool

// An error in the build program itself is all there is to report: nothing says what the
// executables are.
